WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.240
The thing that will keep you going
through the hard times

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.680
is the fact that you really believe
in what you're doing.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.080
So my first tip is find your passion.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.680
Mumsnet took
a really long time to take off

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.120
in any business sense.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.520
In those days, it was all about young
guys being invested in by young guys,

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.160
and here was I turning up,
a 30-year-old mum,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.240
probably with some vomit
on my shoulder.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.760
And I remember one guy said,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.920
"I will invest in your business,
but only if someone else runs it."

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.120
And in fact that someone
was a 24-year-old man.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.000
So I turned down his investment,
but actually,

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.640
you know, when you really
believe in something

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.040
that's what will keep you going
through the low moments.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.760
So choose something
you have a real passion about,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.160
because otherwise I think
it's too easy to give up.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.080
My second tip is to make mistakes.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.200
In fact, Mumsnet was born
out of a mistaken holiday.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.560
It was my first holiday with kids
I knew nothing about it.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.360
And I picked the wrong destination,
the wrong time zone,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.040
the wrong resort. And it was
an unmitigated disaster -

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.960
and that was where the light bulb
moment for Mumsnet came.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.840
Often the things that go wrong

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.840
can be the prompts
for what you can do right.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.920
So my next tip is to wear trainers.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:27.120
I think it's a brilliant way to fit
in exercise without going to the gym.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.240
And it's a brilliant way to catch up
if you're running late.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.280
There's also another part of this,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.520
so don't feel,
as a women in business,

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.720
you have to spend hours
on your appearance.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.560
Let's face it, Mark Zuckerberg wears
the same T-shirt and jeans every day,

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.040
and why should women
have a disadvantage?

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.200
And my final tip
is to embrace the chaos.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.720
I think it's almost impossible
to fit in everything you want to

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.640
if you're trying to start
your own business

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.600
and you want to raise a family.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.840
You have to embrace the fact
that you cannot be perfect.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.920
But more importantly I think, it's
about not feeling guilty about stuff.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.480
So my fourth child,
I cycled to his nursery,

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.520
with him in a seat on the back,

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.280
and he started singing
this lovely little tune to me.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.000
He sang "Mummy, Mummy, Mummy, Mum,
Mummy, Mummy, don't got to work."

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.080
And, quite frankly,
if that had been my first children

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.960
I would have probably
been in tears on the pavement.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.360
But you do get a bit wiser,
your kids will be fine,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.040
and having guilt is a wasted emotion.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.080
I think the thing that makes me
get up in the morning,

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.120
18 years on, and love coming
and doing what I do,

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.840
is I really quite like
finding solutions to things.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.400
Being able to come to work
and collectively,

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.320
with a group of great people,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.680
grapple with stuff
and try and find a solution

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.920
is something I find fascinating,

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.280
and it's what keeps me going really.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:03.000
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

